__registerContent("quickrecall/polity/presidents", {"notes":{"qr-presidents":{"era":"Quick Recall — Polity & Governance","significance":["The chronological order of Presidents with their tenures is a high-frequency Prelims fact and a common 'match the following' target","Several Presidents are associated with unique 'firsts' and constitutional episodes (acting Presidents, uncontested election, death in office) that are directly tested","Knowing who was President during key events (Emergency 1975, dissolution episodes) supports both Prelims and interview preparation"],"features":[{"key":"The 15 Presidents in order","main":"1. Dr. Rajendra Prasad (1950–1962)\n2. Dr. Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan (1962–1967)\n3. Dr. Zakir Husain (1967–1969)\n4. V. V. Giri (1969–1974)\n5. Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed (1974–1977)\n6. Neelam Sanjiva Reddy (1977–1982)\n7. Giani Zail Singh (1982–1987)\n8. R. Venkataraman (1987–1992)\n9. Dr. Shankar Dayal Sharma (1992–1997)\n10. K. R. Narayanan (1997–2002)\n11. Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam (2002–2007)\n12. Pratibha Patil (2007–2012)\n13. Pranab Mukherjee (2012–2017)\n14. Ram Nath Kovind (2017–2022)\n15. Droupadi Murmu (2022–present)","note":"Tenure of the President is 5 years (Article 56)."},{"key":"Key 'firsts' and records","main":"Rajendra Prasad: 1st President; only person to serve two full terms.\nS. Radhakrishnan: 1st Vice-President to become President; also a renowned philosopher.\nZakir Husain: 1st Muslim President; 1st President to die in office.\nV. V. Giri: only person elected as President as an independent candidate; had earlier served as Acting President.\nNeelam Sanjiva Reddy: youngest President; elected unopposed (uncontested).\nPratibha Patil: 1st woman President.\nDroupadi Murmu: 1st tribal woman President and youngest to hold the office.","note":"A. P. J. Abdul Kalam is popularly called the 'People's President' and 'Missile Man of India'."},{"key":"Acting Presidents","main":"India has had three Acting Presidents: V. V. Giri and M. Hidayatullah (following the deaths of Zakir Husain), and B. D. Jatti (during V. V. Giri's succession period). Acting Presidents stepped in when the office fell vacant due to death.","note":"The Vice-President acts as President when a vacancy arises (Article 65)."}],"traps":[{"label":"Who died in office","lines":["Two Presidents died in office: Dr. Zakir Husain (1969) and Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed (1977).","Zakir Husain was the FIRST President to die in office."]},{"label":"Uncontested vs Independent","lines":["Neelam Sanjiva Reddy was elected UNOPPOSED (uncontested) in 1977.","V. V. Giri was the only President elected as an INDEPENDENT candidate — do not confuse the two facts."]},{"label":"Two full terms","lines":["Only Dr. Rajendra Prasad served TWO full terms (1950–1962).","No other President has served two terms."]}],"mainsAngle":"While the President of India is a constitutional head who acts on the aid and advice of the Council of Ministers (Article 74), individual incumbents have shaped the office through discretion during hung verdicts, pocket vetoes and moral authority — illustrating that even a nominal executive carries real weight in a parliamentary democracy.","mainsTheme":"The office of the President — nominal executive, real constitutional significance","recall":["1st President: Rajendra Prasad (only two-term President)","1st Muslim & 1st to die in office: Zakir Husain","Only independent candidate elected: V. V. Giri","Elected unopposed: Neelam Sanjiva Reddy","1st woman President: Pratibha Patil (2007)","1st tribal woman President: Droupadi Murmu (2022)","Presidential term: 5 years (Article 56)"]}},"quizzes":{"qr-presidents":{"title":"Presidents of India (Full List)","questions":[{"q":"Who was the first President of India?","options":["Dr. S. Radhakrishnan","Dr. Rajendra Prasad","Dr. Zakir Husain","V. V. Giri"],"correct":1,"explain":"Dr. Rajendra Prasad was the first President of India (1950–1962) and the only President to serve two full terms."},{"q":"Which President of India was the first to die in office?","options":["Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed","Zakir Husain","V. V. Giri","Neelam Sanjiva Reddy"],"correct":1,"explain":"Dr. Zakir Husain (President 1967–1969) was the first President to die in office. Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed also later died in office (1977)."},{"q":"Which President was the only person to be elected to the office as an independent candidate?","options":["Neelam Sanjiva Reddy","V. V. Giri","R. Venkataraman","K. R. Narayanan"],"correct":1,"explain":"V. V. Giri is the only person elected President as an independent candidate (1969). He had earlier served as Acting President."},{"q":["Consider the following statements:","I. Neelam Sanjiva Reddy was elected President unopposed.","II. Pratibha Patil was the first woman President of India.","Which of the statements given above is/are correct?"],"options":["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"correct":2,"explain":"Both are correct. Neelam Sanjiva Reddy was elected unopposed in 1977, and Pratibha Patil became India's first woman President in 2007."},{"q":"Droupadi Murmu, who assumed office in 2022, is notable as:","options":["The first woman President of India","The first tribal woman President of India","The first President to be elected unopposed","The first Vice-President to become President"],"correct":1,"explain":"Droupadi Murmu is the first tribal woman President of India and the youngest person to hold the office."},{"q":"Which President of India served two full terms in office?","options":["Dr. S. Radhakrishnan","Dr. Rajendra Prasad","Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam","R. Venkataraman"],"correct":1,"explain":"Only Dr. Rajendra Prasad served two full terms (1950–1962). No other President has served two terms."},{"q":"Dr. S. Radhakrishnan holds which of the following distinctions?","options":["First President to die in office","First Vice-President to be elevated to the office of President","First President elected as an independent","First tribal President"],"correct":1,"explain":"Dr. S. Radhakrishnan was the first Vice-President to become President (1962–1967). A noted philosopher, his birthday (5 September) is observed as Teachers' Day."},{"q":"What is the term of office of the President of India under Article 56?","options":["4 years","5 years","6 years","No fixed term"],"correct":1,"explain":"Under Article 56, the President holds office for a term of five years from the date of entering office."},{"q":"Which President is popularly known as the 'Missile Man of India' and the 'People's President'?","options":["K. R. Narayanan","Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam","R. Venkataraman","Pranab Mukherjee"],"correct":1,"explain":"Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam (President 2002–2007) is called the 'Missile Man of India' and the 'People's President'."},{"q":"Which of the following Presidents was the youngest to be elected to the office (among the earlier Presidents) and was elected unopposed?","options":["Giani Zail Singh","Neelam Sanjiva Reddy","V. V. Giri","Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed"],"correct":1,"explain":"Neelam Sanjiva Reddy was the youngest President among the earlier ones and was elected unopposed in 1977."},{"q":"Arrange the following Presidents in correct chronological order of assuming office:\n1. K. R. Narayanan  2. Giani Zail Singh  3. Pranab Mukherjee  4. R. Venkataraman","options":["2, 4, 1, 3","4, 2, 3, 1","2, 1, 4, 3","1, 2, 4, 3"],"correct":0,"explain":"The order is Giani Zail Singh (1982), R. Venkataraman (1987), K. R. Narayanan (1997), Pranab Mukherjee (2012) — i.e. 2, 4, 1, 3."},{"q":["Consider the following statements:","I. Two Presidents of India died in office.","II. Dr. Zakir Husain was the first President to die in office.","Which of the statements given above is/are correct?"],"options":["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"correct":2,"explain":"Both are correct. Dr. Zakir Husain (1969) and Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed (1977) died in office, and Zakir Husain was the first to do so."},{"q":"Who was the President of India during the National Emergency proclaimed in 1975?","options":["V. V. Giri","Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed","Neelam Sanjiva Reddy","Giani Zail Singh"],"correct":1,"explain":"Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed was the President who proclaimed the National Emergency in 1975."},{"q":"Under which Article does the Vice-President act as President when a vacancy arises in the office?","options":["Article 56","Article 60","Article 65","Article 74"],"correct":2,"explain":"Under Article 65, the Vice-President acts as President when the office falls vacant due to death, resignation, removal or otherwise."},{"q":"Who among the following served as an Acting President of India?","options":["Dr. S. Radhakrishnan","M. Hidayatullah","R. Venkataraman","Pratibha Patil"],"correct":1,"explain":"M. Hidayatullah served as Acting President, as did V. V. Giri and B. D. Jatti at different times."},{"q":"Match List-I (President) with List-II (Distinction) and select the correct answer:\nA. Pratibha Patil  B. Droupadi Murmu\n1. First tribal woman President  2. First woman President","options":["A-2, B-1","A-1, B-2","A-2, B-2","A-1, B-1"],"correct":0,"explain":"Pratibha Patil was the first woman President (2007) and Droupadi Murmu the first tribal woman President (2022). Hence A-2, B-1."},{"q":"Which President immediately preceded Droupadi Murmu in office?","options":["Pranab Mukherjee","Ram Nath Kovind","Pratibha Patil","Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam"],"correct":1,"explain":"Ram Nath Kovind (2017–2022) was the President immediately before Droupadi Murmu (2022–present)."},{"q":["Consider the following statements:","I. V. V. Giri had served as Acting President before being elected President.","II. He was the only person elected President as an independent candidate.","Which of the statements given above is/are correct?"],"options":["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"correct":2,"explain":"Both are correct. V. V. Giri first served as Acting President and then, in 1969, became the only person elected President as an independent candidate."},{"q":"Who was the third President of India?","options":["V. V. Giri","Dr. Zakir Husain","Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed","Dr. S. Radhakrishnan"],"correct":1,"explain":"Dr. Zakir Husain (1967–1969) was the third President of India and the first Muslim to hold the office."},{"q":"Statement I: The President of India acts on the aid and advice of the Council of Ministers.\nStatement II: This is provided under Article 74 of the Constitution.\nWhich one of the following is correct?","options":["Both Statement I and Statement II are correct, and II explains I","Both are correct, but II does not explain I","Statement I is correct, but Statement II is incorrect","Statement I is incorrect, but Statement II is correct"],"correct":0,"explain":"Both are correct and II explains I — Article 74 mandates that the President act on the aid and advice of the Council of Ministers headed by the Prime Minister."}]}}});
